<title>INDIA: INDIA'S UNITED FRONT CORE PANEL STARTS MEETING.</title>
<headline>INDIA'S UNITED FRONT CORE PANEL STARTS MEETING.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1997-08-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Leaders of India's ruling United Front coalition on Wednesday began a meeting to consider raising the prices of some petroleum products, officials said.</p>
<p>The alliance's &quot;core committee&quot; was meeting at Prime Minister Inder Kumar Gujral's official residence, they said.</p>
<p>The United Front's decision-making Steering Committee, which is a larger panel including all members of the core committee, was scheduled to meet at 7 p.m. (1330 GMT) and also take up a possible oil price rise.</p>
<p>-- New Delhi Newsroom (91) 11-301-2024; Fax (91) 11-301-4043</p>
